{"id": 39, "ts": 1780473298.7455435, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I\u2019m inclined to side with Sarah and recommend **Candidate\u202fC**. While James rightly highlights B\u2019s strong conscientiousness, stress resilience, and technical aptitude, the documented weak memory for numbers is a concrete attention\u2011and\u2011accuracy risk on long\u2011haul flights where precise calculations are non\u2011negotiable. Moreover, B\u2019s \u201cnasty remarks\u201d about colleagues raise concerns about professional communication and crew cohesion that are harder to remediate than a communication style issue. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC is described as **100\u202f% reliable**, creates a **positive crew atmosphere**, **makes correct decisions quickly**, and possesses **excellent attention skills**\u2014all directly aligned with our core criteria of reliability, decision quality, and information accuracy. Although C has difficulty communicating ideas and is seen as egocentric, these behavioral traits are more amenable to coaching and mentorship than the fundamental numerical\u2011memory deficit we see in B. Therefore, C\u2019s overall safety\u2011critical profile appears stronger for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
