{"id": 48, "ts": 1780473420.2626362, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s confidence in Candidate\u202fB\u2019s technical aptitude and stress handling, but I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the safer overall choice for a long\u2011distance pilot.\u202fC\u2019s record shows **100\u202f% reliability**, a **consistently positive crew atmosphere**, and the ability to **make correct decisions quickly**\u2014all core to operational reliability, crew cooperation, and decision quality on international routes.\u202fWhile B\u2019s \u201cvery conscientious\u201d nature and strong weather\u2011assessment skills are valuable, his **weak memory for numbers** presents a concrete attention\u2011and\u2011accuracy risk that cannot be overlooked on long\u2011haul flights where precise calculations are non\u2011negotiable.\u202fMoreover, B\u2019s documented **grumpy, uncooperative behavior and nasty remarks** directly threaten professional communication and crew cohesion, which are harder to remediate than a numeric\u2011memory deficit that can be mitigated with procedural cross\u2011checks.\u202fC\u2019s communication challenges\u2014difficulty articulating ideas and an egocentric style\u2014are certainly concerns, yet they are behavioral traits that can be addressed through targeted training and mentorship, especially given his proven reliability and crew\u2011building strengths.\u202fUntil we have evidence that B\u2019s numeric\u2011memory issue can be fully mitigated, I will continue to recommend **Candidate\u202fC** as the stronger overall fit."}
